One of my preferred methods: use a boulder to fill the moat diagonal
from the drawbridge, then stay one space to the left so that you are a
knight's move from the portcullis square, burn-engrave Elbereth, from
a few squares distance zap the drawbridge (as stated above,
Shopkeepers carry wands of striking), then use a cockatrice corpse to
fight those who rush out of the front.  The corpse should only last
about 200 turns so get set up first.

By the way, are any of the castle dragons grey?  If so, use a scroll
of earth to fill half the pits to see if the dragon leaves scales.  If
it is grey, but doesn't leave scales, you might as well use up your
wands of undead turning on the (reduced) chance it will leave
scales.

Don't bother killing wraiths in the valley of the dead, they rarely
leave corpses.  You need to lure them to a non-graveyard level (the
castle is a graveyard level, btw)



